{"chunk_id": "f7bcaa720e71", "text": "Yudhishthira resolves to undertake the grand Rajasuya sacrifice and sends a messenger to invite Krishna from Dwaraka. Krishna arrives swiftly at Indraprastha and is warmly received by Yudhishthira, Bhima, Kunti, and the Pandava brothers. After resting, Krishna hears Yudhishthira\u2019s wish to perform the Rajasuya, though the king humbly asks Krishna to judge whether it is truly wise. In response, Krishna explains the political reality of the time: many Kshatriya kings have fallen under the dominance of the powerful Magadhan ruler Jarasandha. Numerous rulers\u2014either through fear or allegiance\u2014serve him, making him the central obstacle to imperial sovereignty. Krishna\u2019s speech reframes the Rajasuya not as a ritual desire but as a political challenge: Yudhishthira cannot claim universal kingship while Jarasandha still dominates the Kshatriya world.\nKrishna arrives at Indraprastha and tells Yudhishthira that Jarasandha\u2019s dominance over many kings blocks the Rajasuya sacrifice unless he is defeated.\nThemes: Rajasuya ambition, imperial legitimacy, Jarasandha\u2019s supremacy, political alliances, Krishna\u2019s counsel", "vector": [0.005753370001912117, -0.025002464652061462, -0.0024762183893471956, 0.011853811331093311, -0.0037743975408375263, 0.01011178083717823, -0.02106454223394394, -0.004845645744353533, -0.011373250745236874, -0.0062072318978607655, 0.008376426063477993, -0.006417477037757635, 0.014563634991645813, -0.0035207688342779875, -0.004158177878707647, -0.0018488207133486867, 0.04952436685562134, -0.015444661490619183, 0.03793753311038017, -0.019796397536993027, 0.0016410787357017398, -0.03379938006401062, 0.0037510369438678026, 0.017487041652202606, -0.017713971436023712, 0.03158346563577652, 0.029340852051973343, -0.01366925984621048, 0.0015025839675217867, 0.007101607508957386, -0.010512247681617737, 0.004865669179707766, -0.005489729344844818, -0.000444267614511773, -0.02835303358733654, 0.0026